Republicans and Democrats in Congress  announced overnight that they reached an  agreement on a massive spending bill  some of the president Trump's key  policies are not included the one  trillion dollar bill would fund the  government through September Nancy  Cordes is on Capitol Hill Nancy good  morning good morning both parties are  calling this a good agreement with  Democrats in particular crowing about  the fact that they managed to block some  of president Trump's key demands for  instance the deal includes 1.5 billion  dollars for more border security but the  bill specifically states that the money  cannot be used to build a new border  wall the bill keeps funding for Planned  Parenthood in place through September  and Democrats say that it keeps 99% of  funding for the EPA an agency that Trump  mr. Trump had vowed to gut on defense  there is a bump in military spending of  fourteen point eight billion dollars  about half of the 30 billion that the  White House had been asking for other  notable features of the spending package  it permanently extends health care  coverage for coal miners and it provides  sixty eight million dollars to help  reimburse local police forces for their  role in protecting President Trump when  he travels to his homes in New York and  Florida this is the first big bipartisan  piece of legislation moving forward  since President Trump took office and  we're expecting Charlie that the House  and Senate will vote on it early this  week ante
 

